## 1. Scope

### 1.1 Covered: licensed under CC-BY 4.0

Each path in this list is covered. A path ending in "/" is a directory:
the data files in it are covered, and it holds a NOTICE.md stating these
terms, so that a copy of the directory carries them. The README.md and
NOTICE.md files in a covered directory are documentation, not data, and
this file does not license them. A path ending in ".py" is a code module:
only the hand-written item literals it names are covered, the code around
them is MIT, and the module's header says so.

- `aidd_docs/results/`: the published results directory. Covers the reference bundle's row files listed below and any record a project command publishes into it, such as the use-case coverage record (`use-case-coverage.json`), in every case except the model-generated content they hold, which 1.3 governs.
- `aidd_docs/results/runtime-reference.jsonl`: the reference bundle's current runtime rows.
- `aidd_docs/results/quality-reference.jsonl`: the reference bundle's current quality rows, including the hand-written suite items they carry in their item fields (`item_id`, `prompt`, `expected_label`, and `reference_output` on graded rows); the model-output fields excepted, see 1.3.
- `aidd_docs/results/runtime-reference.schema-1.jsonl`: superseded runtime rows, retained beside the current ones.
- `aidd_docs/results/quality-reference.schema-1.jsonl`: superseded quality rows, retained beside the current ones, item fields included; the model-output fields excepted, see 1.3.
- `aidd_docs/results/fiches/`: the hardware fiches the rows cite by `fiche_hash`.
- `aidd_docs/results/suite-definitions/`: the published suite-definition snapshots the rows cite by `suite_id` and `suite_version`, including the hand-written suite items as published.
- `aidd_docs/results/comparisons/`: the paired-comparison family records computed over the published rows.
- `aidd_docs/roster/`: the model roster's directory.
- `aidd_docs/roster/models.json`: the model roster the rows cite by `roster_entry_id`, including each entry's licence block and language claim as records. The licences those blocks record are not granted here; see 1.2.
- `src/wave_local_ai_v2/suite_data/`: the hand-written suite items as stored in the source tree, one suite definition per file.
- `src/wave_local_ai_v2/use_case_coverage.json`: the declared use-case coverage record, the source of the copy published into `aidd_docs/results/`.
- `src/wave_local_ai_v2/judge_probe.py`: its hand-written item literals only (`JUDGE_PROBE_ITEMS`).

### 1.2 Not covered: not licensed by this file

- The code, including the code around the item literals in
  `src/wave_local_ai_v2/judge_probe.py`: licensed under the MIT License,
  see LICENSE.
- The untracked per-machine stores `aidd_docs/results/runtime.jsonl` and
  `aidd_docs/results/quality.jsonl`: the live files each machine's runs
  append to. They are not published, not tracked, and not covered, although
  they sit in a covered directory.
- Model weights: the GGUF files the roster points to are not in this
  repository and are not its to license. Their publishers license them.
- The third-party licences the roster records: each roster entry's
  `licence` block records the terms its model's publisher states and when
  they were read. The record is covered (1.1); the model it describes is
  not, and this file grants none of those terms.
- Model-generated content, the model-output fields of the rows included:
  a separate part, stated in 1.3.

### 1.3 The model-output fields: a separate part

This part is every piece of content a model generated rather than the
repository's author, wherever it appears in a covered path: in a row, in a
record a project command publishes, or in any other covered file. In the
published rows today it is one field, `predicted_label`; any field a later
row or record carries that holds a model's generated output (a subject's
generated text, a judge's verdict) joins it.

This content is not licensed under CC-BY 4.0 by this file, even where the
file or directory holding it is covered. It is redistributed on the
author's declaration that redistributing it is permitted. That declaration is unverified against each model's
licence and each provider's terms, and stays unverified until the spike
`aidd_docs/backlog/spikes/may-the-model-outputs-in-the-published-rows-be-redistributed-and-on-what-terms.md`
concludes. Whoever reuses this content does so on their own reading of
those terms.


## 2. Drawn items

The bundle holds no item drawn from a public benchmark today. Every item
in the suite-definition snapshots and in `src/wave_local_ai_v2/suite_data/`
declares `provenance` `hand_written` and carries no `source`, and so does
every row of `quality-reference.jsonl`. The superseded
`quality-reference.schema-1.jsonl` rows predate the provenance fields and
declare none; their items are the same hand-written items.

An item drawn from a public benchmark is not covered by CC-BY 4.0 through
this file. It carries its source's licence, recorded per item in its
`licence`, `source` and `source_revision` fields, and this section names
each drawn source and its terms once the first drawn item is published.
None is listed today.


